# FlexicaAI scheduled jobs — install to /etc/cron.d/flexicaai (mode 0644, root-owned).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: on a self-managed Linux server nothing schedules the job
# endpoints for us. If this is not installed, recalls and appointment reminders
# simply never fire — and NOTHING reports it, because a job that is never invoked
# produces no error to report. This is the single easiest thing to forget when
# deploying, and the failure is silent for weeks. (CLAUDE.md §2a.)
#
# `vercel.json` is inert on this deployment; these schedules are the live ones and
# mirror it so the two don't drift.
#
# ── STATUS: HELD (2026-08-21) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not installed yet, by the owner's direction — safe while there are no live clinics,
# since all six jobs are then no-ops. Install in two parts as the triggers arrive:
#   WhatsApp keys      -> recalls, reminders   (the only two needing an API; no cron
#                                               touches Whisper or Claude)
#   First live clinic  -> expenses, company-expenses, billing, reconcile  (pure DB,
#                                               gated on real data rather than keys)
# Do not let `reconcile` slip past the first PAYING clinic: the payment path is
# deliberately best-effort because this repairs ledger drift nightly (ADR-016).
#
# ── Install ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   sudo install -m 0644 -o root -g root deploy/flexicaai.cron /etc/cron.d/flexicaai
#   sudo install -m 0600 -o root -g root <secret file> /etc/flexicaai/cron.env
#   # /etc/flexicaai/cron.env contains exactly:  CRON_SECRET=<the value from .env>
#
# ── Notes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# * Calls 127.0.0.1 directly, NOT the public hostname: the job never traverses
#   nginx (no proxy_read_timeout, no TLS handshake) and the secret never leaves the
#   loopback interface.
# * `-f` makes curl exit non-zero on an HTTP error, so cron emails/logs a failure
#   instead of silently succeeding on a 401/503. `-s -S` = quiet but keep errors.
# * Times are in the SERVER'S timezone — the same clock availability and
#   "tomorrow" reminders read from. Check it with `timedatectl` before trusting
#   the 09:00/18:00 slots, and pin it to the clinics' region.
# * Output goes to syslog; the app's own structured JSON logs land in journald via
#   the service's stdout (`journalctl -u flexicaai`).

SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
# Set MAILTO to get cron failures by mail; leave empty to rely on syslog only.
MAILTO=""
BASE=http://127.0.0.1:3000

# Recalls: patients due for a follow-up visit.                      09:00 daily
0 9 * * *   flexica  . /etc/flexicaai/cron.env; curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$BASE/api/cron/recalls" >/dev/null

# Day-before appointment reminders.                                 18:00 daily
0 18 * * *  flexica  . /etc/flexicaai/cron.env; curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$BASE/api/cron/reminders" >/dev/null

# Recurring clinic expenses → materialise the ones now due.         02:00 daily
0 2 * * *   flexica  . /etc/flexicaai/cron.env; curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$BASE/api/cron/expenses" >/dev/null

# Recurring FlexicaAI company expenses.                             02:05 daily
5 2 * * *   flexica  . /etc/flexicaai/cron.env; curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$BASE/api/cron/company-expenses" >/dev/null

# Subscription billing sweep: active ↔ past_due as time passes.     03:00 daily
0 3 * * *   flexica  . /etc/flexicaai/cron.env; curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$BASE/api/cron/billing" >/dev/null

# Sales reconciliation: re-derive any drifted ledger row.            03:30 daily
30 3 * * *  flexica  . /etc/flexicaai/cron.env; curl -fsS -m 300 -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" "$BASE/api/cron/reconcile" >/dev/null

# ── Verifying it works ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run one by hand first; a healthy job answers 200 with {"ok":true,...}:
#   curl -fsS -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/cron/recalls
# Then confirm the app logged the run (it records every completion with a timing):
#   journalctl -u flexicaai --since "10 min ago" | grep '"op":"cron.'
# A 401 means the secret doesn't match; a 503 means CRON_SECRET isn't set on the
# APP process, which makes it refuse to run unprotected in production.
